Package: dust
Type: Package
Title: Fast Multiple Change-Point Detection Using the DUST Pruning Method
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Simon", "Querné", email = "simon.querne@gmail.com", role = c("aut")),
    person("Vincent", "Runge", email = "vincent.runge@univ-evry.fr", role = c("aut", "cre")),
        person("Félix", "Laplante", email = "felixlaplante0@proton.me", role = c("aut")),
    person("Charles", "Truong", email = "ctruong@ens-paris-saclay.fr", role = c("ctb"))
            )
Maintainer: Vincent Runge <vincent.runge@univ-evry.fr>
Description: Implements DUST pruning for multiple change-point detection
    in univariate and independent multivariate time series. Includes eight
    one-parameter cost models and a Gaussian model with changes in both mean
    and variance. Multivariate pruning uses selected earlier change-point
    candidates. Scalar and optional Google Highway backends support one-shot
    and incremental analysis. The pruning
    method is described by Runge, Truong and Querné (2025)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2507.02467>.
URL: https://github.com/vrunge/dust
BugReports: https://github.com/vrunge/dust/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.10), methods
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp
SystemRequirements: Optionally, 'Google Highway' (libhwy,
    <https://github.com/google/highway>) for SIMD acceleration. The package
    also builds with a scalar backend when Highway is unavailable.
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
